{number: 74}
{title: I Must Tell Jesus}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] I must tell Jesus all of my trials;
I cannot bear these [Bb7] burdens a-[Eb] lone;
In my distress He kindly will help me;
He ever [Bb7] loves and cares for His [Eb] own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I must tell [Ab] Jesus! I must tell [Eb] Jesus!
I cannot bear my [Bb7] burdens a-[Eb] lone;
I must tell [Ab] Jesus! I must tell [Eb] Jesus!
Jesus can [Bb7] help me, Jesus a-[Eb] lone.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] I must tell Jesus all of my troubles;
He is a kind, com-[Bb7] passionate [Eb] Friend;
If I but ask Him, He will deliver,
Make of my [Bb7] troubles quickly an [Eb] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Tempted and tried, I need a great Savior,
One who can help my [Bb7] burdens to [Eb] bear;
I must tell Jesus, I must tell Jesus;
He all my [Bb7] cares and sorrows will [Eb] share.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [Eb] how the world to evil allures me!
O how my heart is [Bb7] tempted to [Eb] sin!
I must tell Jesus, and He will help me
Over the [Bb7] world the victory to [Eb] win.
{end_of_verse}
